AlphaServer 2000 5/250 System

HIGHLIGHTS

*  AlphaServer 2000 5/250 system manages up to 2,250 transactions per
   minute, with up to 2 symmetric multiprocessing Alpha 21164 processors
*  The introduction of AlphaServer 2000 5/250 systems coincides with the
   release of the Windows NT version of the AlphaServer 2100 5/250 systems
*  Price reductions on current AlphaServer systems and memory options make
   these award winning servers more affordable and competitive

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital is enhancing its award-winning AlphaServer family with the addition
of the AlphaServer 2000 5/250 system, a complementary model that supports up
to two 21164 processors with symmetric multiprocessing. This new model
continues the tradition of delivering leadership performance, as well as
providing cost effective processor upgrades. It is binary compatible with
the other members of the AlphaServer family, and is covered by Digital's
superior three-year, onsite, next-business-day-response-time hardware
warranty. These systems all use the same industry-standard PCI and EISA I/O,
deliver the same advanced reliability and availability features, and support
Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1), OpenVMS, and Windows NT Server
software environments.

The AlphaServer 2000 5/250 has the same characteristics as the other
AlphaServer 2000 systems, but provides significantly increased performance
through its use of the new Alpha 21164 microprocessor, at 250 MHz chip with
a 4 MB third level (off chip) cache.  The AlphaServer 2000 4/200, 4/233, and
4/275 may be upgraded to the faster processor through a simple, cost
effective processor board swap. Memory is compatible through the line. There
is no need to upgrade memory to use the 21164 microprocessor.

BENEFITS

In today's highly competitive, rapidly changing business climate, critical
applications require more from the systems that support them. In particular,
users and managers demand that two critical factors be met by their
computing environments.  These factors are:

*  Users want technological superiority that achieves:
   - Quick response times
   - Fast application processing
   - Uninterrupted service

*  Information technology managers and system managers demand a computing
   environment that:
   - Satisfies users
   - Can grow with their businesses by expanding incrementally and cost
     effectively as the business grows
   - Assures the preservation of current information technology investments

AlphaServer 2000 systems are optimized to meet these computing requirements
by providing exceptional throughput to meet rigorous application processing
needs. This is achievable because of their:

*  Alpha central processors
*  Symmetric multiprocessing (SMP) with up to two processors
*  High performance, industry-standard PCI I/O

Furthermore, cost effective, incremental expansion of system capacity as
computing requirements increase is achievable because of in-cabinet
processor upgrades to ever faster Alpha processors.

Users demand that systems and data be available all the time. The
AlphaServer 2000 systems address this requirement with:

*  A range of high-reliability functions built into the systems
*  A cost effective storage subsystem incorporating up to eight hot swap
   disks and controller-based RAID to provide very high data integrity

When users outgrow two processor SMP, they can further expand their systems
by clustering multiple AlphaServer 2000 systems together. This adds the
additional benefit of going beyond high reliability and into high
availability.  Digital is the industry leader and the inventor of cluster
technology.

With this scope of capabilities, AlphaServer 2000 systems deliver high
productivity for business operations, cost effective solutions for computing
challenges, and safeguards for valuable business information.

Warranty

Digital's hardware warranty for the AlphaServer systems leads the
competition. Digital's hardware warranty is three years onsite,
five-days-by-nine hours, with next-business-day response time. Compared to
warranties for the major UNIX systems, the AlphaServer bundled hardware
warranty provides support for a longer period of time, with better response
time, from a large number of international locations. (For specific details
on Digital's AlphaServer warranties and where they offer a competitive
advantage, please refer to the "New Warranty and Service Offerings for
AlphaStation and AlphaServer Systems" article in the November 1994 issue of
Customer Update.)

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

All versions of the AlphaServer 2000 5/250 systems (Digital UNIX, OpenVMS,
and Windows NT Server) can be ordered now and will begin shipping in
mid-August. The Windows NT version of the AlphaServer 2100 5/250 system,
which was announced in April, can also be ordered now and will begin
shipping in mid-August. ( The Digital UNIX and OpenVMS versions of the
AlphaServer 2100 5/250 system, also announced in April, began shipping in
June. Please refer to the "AlphaServer 2100 Systems" article in the April
1995 issue of Customer Update for part number and pricing information for
all AlphaServer 2100 5/250 systems.)

