New Internet AlphaServer System Configurations

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Internet AlphaServer Systems include new pre-configured internet-ready
   web servers optimized for the needs of commercial Internet users
*  The packaged systems now include Digital UNIX Unlimited User Licenses,
   making them ideal platforms for Internet Service providers and for
   internet publishing and authoring
*  New Internet AlphaServer Software Kit V1.2 is included to make
   installation and setup easy

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Internet AlphaServer systems are pre-configured Internet-ready web servers
that put a world of information at users' fingertips and allow them to
publish information to literally millions of other Internet users.

The new Internet AlphaServer systems are the Internet AlphaStation 200
4/100, the Internet AlphaServer 400 4/166, and the Internet AlphaServer 1000
4/233, which replace the existing Internet AlphaServer systems (see the
"Product and Service Retirements" section in this issue for more details).

Internet AlphaServer systems now feature the Internet AlphaServer Software
Kit V1.2, a suite of pre-packaged, pre-ested Internet software that includes
updated versions of the fully-supported Netscape Communications Server
software from Netscape Communications; Digital's ELECTRONIC LOCKER software,
which makes installation and setup easy; and a collection of public software
(see the "Internet AlphaServer Software Kit V1.2" article in this issue).

Internet AlphaServer systems now also include a Digital UNIX Unlimited User
License, which allows unlimited Telnet, FTP, and interactive terminal or
terminal-emulation sessions -- making the systems ideal platforms for
Internet authoring and publishing.

Internet AlphaStation 200 4/100

The performance and value of the new Internet AlphaStation 200 4/100 make it
an outstanding platform for Internet authoring, desktop publishing,
multimedia, and piloting applications for an Internet server. The Internet
AlphaStation 200 4/100 offers exceptional performance at an affordable
price. Housed in a slimline desktop enclosure, the packaged system accepts
industry-standard options running on both PCI and ISA buses. It provides
leadership price/performance, investment protection, and openness; and
supports today's leading commercial Internet applications (desktop
publishing, database management, and multimedia).

Internet AlphaServer 400 4/166

The expandability and upgrade features of the new Internet AlphaServer 400
4/166 make it well suited for publishing information via the Internet, for
use as a listserver or mailserver, or for Internet collaboration and
communication where the need for growth, without investing in a whole new
platform, may be required.

The 166 MHz Alpha uniprocessor server, packaged in a mini-tower enclosure,
is an entry-level Internet server for small to medium-sized businesses and
workgroups. The highly reliable Internet server offers many server specific
features, including security and management, with remote management possible
via a simple serial link. Also, the product has been designed to allow for
future upgrades to faster Alpha processors.

The Internet AlphaServer 400 4/166 supports up to 192 MB of
industry-standard SIMM memory and has an integrated fast SCSI-2 controller.
It also incorporates industry-standard I/O, including one PCI/ISA, two PCI,
and three ISA slots. In addition, it has five drive bays to support over 17
GB of disk storage internally, and over 90 GB with external expansion.

Internet AlphaServer 1000 4/233

The reliability and management features of the Internet AlphaServer 1000
4/233 make it an ideal platform for Internet-accessed information
repositories, for hosting home pages, or for use in Internet commerce, where
there is a need for continuous uptime with little or no onsite support. The
Internet AlphaServer 1000 4/233 is a 233 MHz Alpha uniprocessor server in a
deskside tower enclosure running Digital UNIX, and offering high reliability
features such as fully redundant power supplies, internal RAID, hot swap
disks, a dual SCSI backplane, ECC memory, ECC cache, a temperature sensor, a
power supply sensor, and a fan sensor.

The Internet AlphaServer 1000 4/233 provides support for up to 10 internal
mass storage devices, which include a floppy diskette drive and a CD-ROM.
The server also supports up to 512 MB of RAM, up to 7 hot swap StorageWorks
disk drives, and a tape drive; and will soon support wide SCSI devices. The
server supports over 28 GB of disk storage internally, and up to 440 GB with
external expansion.  PCI-based FDDI, RAID, Ethernet controllers, and
asynchronous multiplexer cards are also supported on the Internet
AlphaServer 1000 4/233. All this expandability, using PC industry-standard
components such as 72-pin 36-bit SIMMs, provides balanced system performance
at an affordable price. Remote diagnosis features of the Internet
AlphaServer 1000 allow resellers and system administrators to call in and
remotely run the diagnostics, configure the system, recommend a fix, or pull
the right part. Support costs are minimized because onsite visits and
service calls are minimized.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Internet AlphaStation 200 4/100, Internet AlphaServer 400 4/166, and
Internet AlphaServer 1000 4/233 are available now.

