Internet AlphaServer Software Kit V1.2

HIGHLIGHTS

*  The software that comes with the Internet AlphaServer family can now be
   ordered as a separate package for Digital UNIX based systems
*  Digital's AlphaServer 2100 system and a wide range of Alpha systems can
   be made application-ready for Internet use
*  Distributors, resellers, and end users now have more opportunity to
   configure systems to meet their unique needs and add their own value

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Internet AlphaServer Software Kit V1.2 provides the capability to
configure a wide range of Alpha systems as Internet servers. With the
software kit, users have access to the full expandability and scalability of
the Alpha systems family.

The Internet AlphaServer Software Kit includes Digital's unique ELECTRONIC
LOCKER administration software for easy management of the server
installation and administration of server and user accounts, all using a
Mosaic-like interface. The kit also includes the Netscape Communications
Server from Netscape Communications. This product provides high-performance,
easy-to-use server software for publishing rich hypertext documents on the
Internet's World Wide Web.

A selection of public software also ships with the Internet AlphaServer
Software Kit V1.2, including:

*  Free WAIS
*  INN Network News Server
*  Tin News Reader
*  CERN World Wide Web server software
*  Pine Mail
*  LYNX

Additionally, the AlphaServer Software Kit contains MailWorks for Digital
UNIX software, which is licensed separately. MailWorks software combines the
reliability and security of host-based mail systems with the flexibility and
ease of use of PC LAN mail systems -- offering better service and a lower
cost than these systems. The kit utilizes the Telnet and FTP Internet
applications supplied by the Digital UNIX operating system, which also
provides a POP3 mail server.

BENEFITS

*  The integrated software kit contains the most commonly used Internet
   applications as well as industry leading Netscape Communications Server
   software.
*  The kit enables users to build Internet servers using a wide range of
   Alpha systems.
*  Distributors and VARs can add value by integrating the optimum hardware,
   software, and applications to meet users' unique needs.
*  From pilot to production, the scalability of Alpha systems allows
   Internet application developers to select a system for their needs now,
   with plenty of options with which to grow in the future.
*  The performance of the 64-bit AlphaServer family and the award winning,
   standards-compliant Digital UNIX operating system create a server that is
   ideal for providing the multimedia capabilities that today's users
   demand.
*  This software kit includes many of the most popular Internet applications
   in the public software repository, including News Reader, News Server,
   and Free WAIS.
*  Digital chose the most feature rich, robust versions of public software
   and tested them on the most popular AlphaServer hardware models. All of
   the software on the CD-ROMs has been consolidated, compiled, tested, and
   integrated for interoperability -- steps typically associated with
   building and debugging software products from scratch. This saves users
   time and money in set up and installation.
*  Digital's ELECTRONIC LOCKER system administration software is included in
   the package for easy management of user accounts, printing, system
   backups, and straightforward user menus.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Internet AlphaServer Software Kit V1.2 is available now. In addition, a
complete range of software support, planning, design, implementation, and
maintenance services that supplement this product is available from Digital
and its resellers; and comprehensive firewall services are also available.

