Frame Technology Products for Digital UNIX Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

*  FrameMaker, FrameViewer, and Frame Developer's Kit V4 products are
   available now on Digital UNIX; FrameMaker V5 will be available for
   Digital UNIX by the end of the calendar year
*  Users who purchase V4 products for Digital UNIX now, with the special
   support offer, will receive a free upgrade to FrameMaker V5

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Frame Technology's FrameMaker products support the complete document
lifecycle, from creation and authoring, revisions and editing, to tracking,
retrieval, electronic distribution, and viewing. Frame's products are
particularly well suited to production of large, complex documents typically
found in engineering, marketing communications, MIS, research and
development, and technical publications departments.

FrameMaker software combines word processing, page layout, graphics,
equations, and book-building tools for efficient creation of a wide range of
publications, from books and technical manuals to reports, newsletters, and
presentations.

FrameViewer software, Frame's electronic document viewing technology,
enables online distribution of documents. It offers significant cost savings
over paper-based distribution, improves access to information through
hypertext navigation, and ensures that organizations have up-to-date, online
information

The Frame Developer's Kit is targeted at end users, independent software
vendor developers, value-added resellers, and systems integrators who want
to create custom applications around Frame's products.

BENEFITS

*  Cross-platform compatibility -- Frame products run on UNIX systems from
   Digital, HP, and Sun, and on Windows-based PCs and Macintosh systems.
   Frame products use a common file format across all computing platforms.
   This unique capability enables users to create documents on an
   AlphaStation system, edit them on other UNIX systems and Windows based
   PCs, and format them on a Macintosh system -- all without the
   inconvenience of file conversions and filters. In this way, Frame
   eliminates the barriers to collaborative authoring and enables workgroups
   to produce better documents in less time.
*  Long document features -- FrameMaker gives users sophisticated control
   over their documents and the ability to automatically manage tedious,
   time consuming tasks such as creating tables of contents, indexes, or
   lists; updating page, chapter, and footnote numbering; and cross
   referencing. Users can also create single, cohesive documents from
   multiple files, allowing multiple authors to collaborate on documents
   easily and efficiently, and to track the difference between two version
   of the same document.
*  Electronic distribution -- Available through FrameMaker's unique
   companion product, FrameViewer, electronic distribution helps companies
   leverage the substantial investment they have made in creating complex
   documents by improving access to document-based information and reducing
   the costly and cumbersome task of printing and distributing paper
   documents.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Frame V4 products are available now on Digital UNIX. FrameMaker V5 will be
available for Digital UNIX by the end of the calendar year.

Annual support contracts are available, which include technical support,
major and minor upgrades, and the technical support newsletter. For volume
support pricing, contact a local Frame sales representative.

