ManageWORKS/HUBwatch PC Based LAN Management Package

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Complete solution manages both the client/server relationship and Digital
   network devices using ManageWORKS and HUBwatch products
*  Click on network map icons for easy management of DEChub and GIGAswitch
   network devices
*  Alarms highlight problem areas
*  One interface provides multivendor network operating system (NOS)
   administration for Novell NetWare, Microsoft LAN Manager, IBM LAN Server,
   and PATHWORKS environments

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The ManageWORKS/HUBwatch package provides users with an unbeatable PC based
LAN management package. ManageWORKS Workgroup Administrator uses the simple
network management protocol (SNMP) to draw a network map, handle alarms, and
browse MIBs, as well as other network management tasks. Through ManageWORKS,
users can manage Novell, Microsoft, IBM, and Digital PC LANs.

When a manager double clicks on a DEChub icon on the network map, HUBwatch
is invoked for powerful, graphical, SNMP management of Digital devices.
HUBwatch lets users create virtual LANs by drawing them. Interconnecting
ports, modules, or LAN segments to create a virtual network in a DEChub 900
MultiSwitch is a simple drag-and-drop operation. Managing a GIGAswitch/FDDI
or GIGAswitch/ATM is equally as easy.

BENEFITS

*  Reduced network management expense -- The ManageWORKS/HUBwatch package
   allows easy monitoring of multiple DEChub networks using a network map
   and alarms, while providing a quick and easy way to examine a device in
   more detail.
*  Lowest cost for full function workgroup management -- Package includes
   workgroup network manager, PC LAN manager, and Digital device manager at
   the lowest cost in the industry.
*  Minimal investment -- Products run on existing PCs, with minimal training
   required to use package.
*  Reduced training for multivendor NOS administration -- Users must learn
   only one interface, instead of individual interfaces
  for each vendor.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The ManageWORKS/HUBwatch package is available now.

