DIGITAL RESELLS NETSCAPE NAVIGATOR V1.2 FOR WINDOWS 95

Digital is now offering Netscape Navigator V1.2 for Windows 95 software as
part of its Internet product portfolio. Designed specifically for the
soon-to-be-released Microsoft Windows 95 operating environment, Netscape
Navigator V1.2 provides the best possible performance, ease of use, and
integration for PC users who wish to take advantage of the new environment.

Netscape Navigator is available for all popular desktop environments. The
powerful commercial Internet browser offers high-performance and secure
point-and-click network navigation. It is optimized to run smoothly over
14.4 kilobit per second modems as well as higher bandwidth lines, delivering
performance up to 10 times that of other network browsers. The software
provides a common feature set and graphical user interface across computers
running the Microsoft Windows, Macintosh, or X Window System operating
environments.

V1.2 runs with Microsoft Windows V3.1 as well as Windows 95, facilitating
users' upgrade to the Windows 95 environment. The software builds on the
success of Netscape Navigator for Digital UNIX, NT Alpha, NT Intel, and DOS
Windows systems. It is one of the first Internet browsers to integrate the
Windows 95 user interface and other advanced features, making it easy for
Windows 95 users to employ the full breadth of Internet commerce and
enterprise applications.

V1.2 features include:

*  Windows 95 interface support:
   - Drag-and-drop URLs.
   - Support for Windows 95 native dialog boxes, such as "Save" and "Print."
*  Integration of  Windows 95 features such as Internet Shortcuts, which
   enable users to create icons to represent Internet URLs. When a shortcut
   is double-clicked, Netscape Navigator software displays the URL.
   Shortcuts can be placed on the desktop or inside folders and directories,
   and can be embedded as mail objects.
*  An enhanced Bookmark interface that provides drag and drop capabilities
   within a hierarchical folder-based interface, making it even easier for
   users to create and maintain a directory of their favorite Internet
   sites.
*  A new interface for FTP downloads, which provides increased feedback to
   users.

For additional information on V1.2, see the "Digital and Netscape
Communications Expand Their Product Portfolio" article in the June issue of
Customer Update.

