Technology Migration Services For Windows 95

HIGHLIGHTS

o  More complex than previous upgrades, Windows 95 requires comprehensive
   hardware, software, and networks assessment before migration

o  Maximum productivity gains come about with the Windows 95 multitasking
   and 32-bit operating system, and good preparation and training to take
   advantage of new features

o  "Service Bridge" closes the technology "time-to-results" gap, minimizes
   disruption and time to complete migration; leaves a fully documented
   environment

PROGRAM DESCRIPTION

Digital's Multivendor Customer Services (MCS) organization has created a
Technology Migration Services (TMS) program especially for the release of
Microsoft's Windows 95 desktop operating system. The goal of this program is
to assist corporate information systems division and business managers to
assess, plan, and implement a detailed, controlled program for this complex
migration. Digital's comprehensive approach combines program management;
technology consulting, systems and application compatibility, user skills
assessment; hardware and software acquisition, installation and upgrades,
and asset recovery. The program has four parts:

o  Managed migration from assessments through post-implementation support
o  Comprehensive readiness assessment
o  Migration process requirements
o  Post-implementation support

TMS answers the widespread need to temporarily increase resources for the
migration effort and to guide organizations through the migration experience
in an orderly fashion with minimal operating downtime and reduced business
disruption.  MCS has taken advantage of its long-term relationship with
Microsoft and beta testing of Windows 95 to pull together a set of services
that make use of a proven program management methodology and years of
complex migration and project implementation experience.

A special Windows 95 Quick Start Pilot Package is available for customers
with 100 desktop computers that meet windows and network requirements. MCS
will acquire the Windows 95 and Office 95 licenses, perform the software and
hardware installations, provide Windows 95 "differences" end user training
in groups of 25, and provide supplemental help desk services for 90 days to
support the pilot.  Users will also get two coupons for technical training.

BENEFITS

The benefits of this technology migration strategy fall into four
categories:

o  Carefully managed migration that includes readiness assessment and
   ensures that implementation occurs on time and within budget

o  Comprehensive readiness assessment
   - Creates individual desktop hardware and software profiles to analyze
     Windows 95 compatibility
   - Creates an asset configuration database
   - Analyzes local and wide area networks existing configuration and
     capacity
   - Develops a training plan for both end user and support staffs

o  Migration process requirements
   - Have technically capable resources ready and available for installation
   - Reconfigure LANs and WANs for Windows 95 interconnectivity and
     increased traffic
   - Provide classroom and onsite training for systems and network
     management, application developers, technical support staffs, and end
     users; at implementation and beyond
   - Provide supplemental help desk support for peak periods

o  Post-implementation support
   - Provide up-to-date asset and desktop management via PC Utility services
   - Manage desktop lifecycle and cost of ownership issues
   - Develop customized JITT (Just-In-Time-Training) programs at all levels

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Technology Migration Services are available now. For more information, call
1-800-888-4234, extension 95; or to arrange a visit, call your local sales
representative or reseller.

