BackOffice Servers

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Agreement with Microsoft to offer the Microsoft BackOffice suite of
   client/server software products on selected AlphaServer systems and Intel
   based Prioris PC servers

o  Single vendor solution for set-up, training, and ongoing support of an
   organization's business-critical applications, including database
   management, IBM SNA host connectivity and remote system management,
   software distribution, and asset management

o  Industry's broadest range of leadership server platforms for Windows NT
   based business solutions

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital has entered into an agreement with Microsoft Corporation to offer a
family of BackOffice Servers that feature Microsoft BackOffice software on
selected AlphaServer systems and Intel based Prioris PC servers.

Microsoft BackOffice is an integrated family of server software built on the
Microsoft Windows NT Server operating system. The family consists of Windows
NT Server as the network foundation, Microsoft SQL Server for managing and
storing data, Microsoft SNA Server for host connectivity, Microsoft Systems
Management Server for managing PCs and servers, and Microsoft Mail Server
for distributing information. BackOffice seamlessly integrates corporate
data with the desktop environment, providing:

o  Links to information regardless of location, including IBM mainframe data

o  Common Windows based systems management and centralized administration of
   distributed resources and server applications

o  Interoperability with Microsoft Office applications across the network

o  Built-in support features for lower support costs

BENEFITS

The Microsoft BackOffice family of server applications has been designed to
work together, making it easier for companies to improve decision-making and
streamline business processes. Digital's ready-to-implement BackOffice
Servers provide users with a powerful platform for cost-effective
client/server computing. These servers feature:

o  Integrated "best-of-class" Windows NT server applications

o  Widest choice of leadership server platforms to meet future growth needs

o  Minimal training time for administrators, users, and developers

o  Simplified management and improved control of distributed computing
   resources

o  A single vendor solution for mission-critical service and support through
   Digital's worldwide enterprise service organization

o  Packaging to maximize value

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

A BackOffice Server includes the BackOffice Server suite of products, which
is composed of Windows NT Server, SQL Server, SNA Server, Systems Management
Server, and Microsoft Mail Server, licensed to one server. All media and
documentation is included in the BackOffice Server software kit and supports
both Intel and AlphaServer systems. The BackOffice Server Models 1000, 2000,
and 2100 are available now. Digital Prioris PC Server pricing and ordering
information will be announced separately.

Several components of the BackOffice software suite may be ordered
individually. Windows NT Server, SQL Server, and Systems Management Server
can be added today to any new Digital server hardware system order. These
products cannot be ordered without a new hardware system order. Software
only orders should be referred to Microsoft distributors or can be ordered
from Digital by organizations with a Microsoft Select Contract.

Order No.      Description

PB71B-AC       BackOffice Server 1000 4/233 120V

PB71B-AD       BackOffice Server 1000 4/233 240V

