               online documentation, server license, 5 client access
	       licenses

QB-3WSAA-SA    Microsoft SNA Server. Includes media, documentation, server
	       license, 5 client access licenses

Licensing BackOffice Servers

Each BackOffice Server is licensed as an entity to a single server; users
cannot "split" server applications across multiple servers. (Note that
BackOffice Servers do not include any Client Access Licenses.)

Users do have flexibility in how they want to license the clients accessing
a BackOffice Server. Microsoft licenses clients under either a "per seat"
model in which every desktop can access any server, or a "per server" model
in which a set number of desktops are allowed access to a particular server.
Users can start out with a "per server" model and make a one-time switch to
a "per seat" model.

A BackOffice Client Access License enables a single desktop to access any
BackOffice Server application on any server. Or users can selectively
license desktops to one or more particular server applications. For example,
a user with 100 desktops accessing a BackOffice Server may choose to provide
all desktops with access to Windows NT Server services, but buy only 25
Client Access Licenses for SQL Server. (Note that SMS Server and Microsoft
Mail offer only a "per seat" Client Access model.)

Client Access Licenses are available only from Microsoft authorized
resellers or from Digital for organizations with a Microsoft Select
Contract.

SERVICES

Digital offers BackOffice Server users a comprehensive portfolio of services
for their client/server environments ranging from planning, design,
implementation, and interoperability services, to product update and
technical support services. Digital is a Microsoft Solution Provider and is
one of three global Authorized Support Center (ASC) partners.

All BackOffice Servers come with a three year onsite hardware warranty.
BackOffice Server systems also include 90 day phone support for system
installation/configuration assistance as part of the system warranty. It is
recommended that, at a minimum, users purchase software update services for
BackOffice Server software. This ensures that users will receive the latest
versions of BackOffice Server software automatically.

Digital's new Help Desk Services Program (available in the U.S. and Canada
in September 1995, with worldwide availability after September 1995) offers
BackOffice Server users both product and problem solving support through
various packaged options best suited to individual user's needs. These
packaged options include Help Desk Pro and Help Desk Premium. The Help Desk
Pro package targets help desk professionals and provides 24 x 7 telephone
technical support, including advice, problem analysis, and resolution. The
Help Desk Premium package targets Level II (technical support) staff, such
as LAN and system managers. This package provides a named account
representative to deliver 24 x 7 business critical environment support. Help
Desk Pro and Help Desk Premium users may purchase this support on a per
incident call pack or a maximum number of incidents on an annual contract
basis. Digital also offers a Custom Help Desk as part of its overall Help
Desk Services Program. The Custom Help Desk is a highly flexible option
targeted at providing users' Level II staff and developers with world class
open client/server solutions.

Digital is a Microsoft Select Reseller, offering users a range of Microsoft
Select Contract options based on individual user needs/requirements. It is
highly recommended that BackOffice Server users purchase a Microsoft Select
Contract from Digital to ensure their client/server environment remains
current at all times.

