Midrange RW532 Optical Library

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Midrange storage options of 38 GB and 76 GB

o  New RW532 library features four magneto-optical drives with storage
   capacity for 64 platters; redesigned RW531 library offers two
   magneto-optical drives and storage capacity for 32 platters

o  Multifunction magneto-optical drives support both rewritable and WORM
   applications

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The new optical libraries, RW532-ZF and RW531-ZC, provide additional options
and flexibility to accommodate ever-increasing demands for higher capacity
online and near-online storage.

The RW532-ZF/MF is a new library offering four magneto-optical drives and
storage capacity for 64 platters (maximum 76 GB with 1.2 GB per platter).
This drive and capacity combination is the new midrange point in the family;
positioned between the RW531 and the current RW534 (4 drives, 88 platters).

The RW531-ZC/MC is a redesigned optical library containing two
magneto-optical drives and storage capacity for 32 platters (maximum of 38
GB with 1.2 per GB platter). It replaces the RW530, which will be retired in
the near future.

RW532-UB is the upgrade kit to convert an RW531-ZC to an RW532-ZF, by adding
two optical drives, storage slots, and a controller board for an additional
32 platters (38 GB with 1.2 GB per platter). This product provides a field
upgrade path in a capacity range where none was available before.

Compared to the RW530, the two new jukeboxes are taller, wider, deeper, and,
therefore, not rackmountable. The new dimensions are 35.8 inches (909 mm)
high, 18.9 inches (480 mm) wide, and 33.8 inches (859 mm) deep. (For more
information, see the "RW525-ZA Optical Library" article in the July 1995
issue of Customer Update).

BENEFITS

o  Lower total cost -- By using an optical jukebox, in which removable media
   share a limited number of physical drives, systems are configured with
   more physical storage at a lower cost than with magnetic disks.

o  Faster performance -- The RW531-ZC and RW532-ZF were redesigned to
   provide faster exchange of optical platters (six seconds average).

o  Greater reliability -- These versions are designed to provide longer mean
   time between failures of the autochanger than earlier versions.

o  Family compatibility -- Internally, the optical libraries use the RWZ52
   drive. This is the same drive used in the current family of RW500
   jukeboxes. Therefore, when a tabletop or StorageWorks RWZ52 optical drive
   and Optical Storage Desktop Software (for either OpenVMS or Digital UNIX
   operating system) are used with a member of the RW500 family, users are
   assured of platter compatibility.

o  Investment protection -- This comes in two forms: first, compatibility
   between devices means the existing platters are included within the
   automated library. Second, the RW531-ZC and RW532-ZF, and the
   recently-announced RW525, will be upgradable to the next generation of
   higher-capacity magneto-optical drives when they become available.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The RW531ZC and RW532ZF are available now.

