AlphaStation 600 5/266 and 5/300 Rackmount Workstations

HIGHLIGHTS

o  AlphaStation 600 5/266 Rackmount workstations offer leadership
   price/performance, expandability, and multiple system integration

o  High-end 64-bit PCI based Alpha client system supports the Digital UNIX,
   OpenVMS, and Windows NT workstation environments; and a PCI I/O bus
   running at 264 MB per second at peak

o  Three-year hardware warranty and 90-day telephone advisory software
   support included

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The AlphaStation 600 Rackmount systems are the first Digital workstations to
use the Alpha 21164 chip. The systems come in a rackmountable chassis that
can be assembled at the factory prior to shipment, for a total integrated
solution, or shipped directly to the user for integration at the user site.
The Rackmount systems are available as system building blocks (SBBs) so they
can be configured to meet users' unique application requirements. Key
features include the capacity to utilize up to 1 GB of ECC memory, six
internal storage slots for up to 17.2 GB of SCSI disk, and eight total
option slots that accept both PCI and EISA options available from Digital
and its business partners. The AlphaStation 600 rackmount systems are ideal
for users who demand high performance and graphics, and require all the
benefits of standard option support in a single cabinet enclosure. They
support the Digital UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1) and OpenVMS operating systems,
and will support Microsoft's Windows NT operating system in the fourth
quarter of 1995.

The AlphaStation 600 5/266 includes an on-board cache of 2 MB (4 MB for the
Model 5/300), a 256-bit wide memory bus, and a 64-bit PCI I/O bus that runs
at 264 MB per second at peak. Performance for these systems is:

o  Model 5/266 -- 288 SPECint92 and 428 SPECfp92
o  Model 5/300 -- 334 SPECint92 and 503 SPECfp92

The AlphaStation 600 Rackmount offers the same functionality and performance
as the deskside system (see the "AlphaStation 600 Family of High Performance
Workstations" article in the August issue of Customer Update).

Upgrade to Rackmount Model 5/300

The AlphaStation 600 5/266 to AlphaStation 600 5/300 upgrade package will
ship in the fourth quarter of 1995. It will be a board swap that Digital's
field service will handle. The upgrade will include a new 4 MB cache as well
as the 300 MHz Alpha 21164. Users who want the 300 MHz system can take
delivery of the AlphaStation 600 5/266 immediately and get the upgrade when
it becomes available later this year.

