Windows NT Workstation 3.51 and Windows NT Server 3.51

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Expanded platform support for the PowerPC, AlphaServer 2100 5/250, and
   AlphaStation 600 systems

o  Provides improvements in Setup, Command Prompt, Windows 95 common
   controls, and Help

o  Windows NT 3.51 has been tested for PCMCIA compatibility -- x86 platform
   only

o  Windows NT Server 3.51 includes two licensing tools: licensing option in
   Control Panel, and License Manager program in the Network Administration
   program group

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Microsoft Windows NT 3.51 is a powerful, advanced, 32-bit, multitasking
operating system that supports Intel (x86) and RISC processors and provides
support for symmetric multiple processors. Windows NT Workstation 3.51 is
the workstation operating system that provides the power of a workstation
with the ease of use, productivity, and compatibility of a personal
computer. Windows NT Server 3.51, the server edition of  the Windows NT
operating system, goes beyond the capabilities of Windows NT Workstation to
provide a network that is easy to set up, manage, and control. Windows NT
Workstation 3.51 and Windows NT Server 3.51 provide improvements in
performance and functionality.

Windows NT 3.51 has the familiar Windows graphics user interface, integrated
networking, and workgroup productivity tools, with added built-in group mail
and scheduling applications. Windows NT is compatible with Windows, MS-DOS,
OS/2, and POSIX applications. It also meets U.S. Government C2 security
requirements.

BENEFITS

o  Windows NT Workstation 3.51 offers system integrity, access to large
   amounts of memory and disk, security, and fault protection required by
   users with mission-critical applications.

o  Windows NT Server 3.51 offers improved performance and connectivity and
   the availability of several new 32 bit server applications that assist
   users who are downsizing their legacy systems to client/server computing
   or upsizing from file sharing systems to client/server computing.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Windows NT 3.51 is shipping now with new Digital systems. Pre-packaged
systems include the Windows NT 3.51 operating system.

The Windows NT 3.51 operating system kits include CD-ROM media, three Setup
Diskettes for Intel based systems, Installation Guide, Update Information
for Version 3.51 book, and appropriate operating systems proof of license.
The kits will also include the "Microsoft Windows NT 3.51 Release Notes for
Digital Alpha Systems" diskette, which contains online release notes for
installing/upgrading to Windows NT 3.51 on all Alpha systems. In addition to
the operating system, users can also order a full kit of documentation for
Windows NT Workstation 3.51 and Windows NT Server 3.51.

Windows NT Workstation 3.51 and Windows NT Server 3.51 Upgrade Kits are
available now also. Kits contain new 3.51 media and the "Update Information
for Version 3.51" book. These kits will contain proof of license only; no
Client Access Licenses will be included. Free Windows NT 3.5 upgrade part
numbers (BR-0QRAC-SA and BR-23CAB-SA) are obsolete.  Windows NT operating
systems must be ordered with the appropriate hardware. A proof of purchase
and proof of license are required when purchasing an Upgrade Kit.

