(2)Windows NT 3.5 Client Access Licenses are valid for Windows NT 3.51.

Digital upgrade/update programs

Users who have purchased Windows NT Workstation 3.5 or Windows NT Server 3.5
from Digital have the following options:

o  Users under a maintenance agreement or who are members of the Select
   Service Program will automatically receive a Windows NT 3.51 Upgrade Kit
   when the kit becomes available.

o  Users can purchase a retail version of the Windows NT 3.51 Upgrade Kit
   from any authorized reseller. Authorized resellers may require proof of
   purchase and proof of license.

o  Digital will also offer a Windows NT 3.5 to Windows NT 3.51 Upgrade Kit.
   Proof of purchase of Windows NT 3.5 is required (such as proof of
   license). Digital's Upgrade Kit will include some additional components
   not found on the retail kits. These components include firmware updates,
   an updated ECU (EISA Configuration Utility), and release notes to
   install/upgrade Windows NT 3.51 onto an Alpha system platform.

In addition, users who have an Alpha system and have a maintenance agreement
or decide to purchase a retail kit may also need to update their firmware.
In most cases this is not required but highly recommended. Users can update
the firmware by:

o  Copying the firmware update kits from CompuServe DEC4WNT forum. The
   firmware updates can be found in the Library Section 4, Hardware
   Information.

o  Copying the firmware update kits from the Internet gatekeeper.dec.com
   using an FTP session. The firmware updates can be found in the following
   area: /private/fwaxp.

o  Ordering the Alpha Systems Update Kit for Windows NT 3.51. This kit
   contains the Alpha AXP Systems Firmware Update CD, the Microsoft Windows
   NT 3.51 Release Notes for Digital Alpha Systems diskette, and the most
   current version of the ECU (EISA Configuration Utility) for Windows NT.

o  Ordering the Windows NT Server or Windows NT Workstation 3.51 Upgrade Kit
   from Digital. Proof of 3.5 License required. The Alpha Systems Update Kit
   components are included in the Windows NT 3.51 Upgrade Kit manufactured
   by Digital.

Microsoft upgrade programs

Microsoft has announced several retail upgrade programs that include free
upgrades, upgrades from Windows NT 3.1 to Windows NT 3.51, and the purchase
of additional Client Access Licenses. The following options exist:

o  Users who purchased a Retail Windows NT Workstation 3.5 or Windows NT
   Server 3.5 after April 15, 1995, can receive a free upgrade directly from
   Microsoft or any Microsoft reseller until the end of August. Proof of
   purchase will be required, and restrictions may apply.

o  Users who purchased Windows NT 3.1 or Windows NT Advanced Server 3.1 must
   upgrade by purchasing the upgrade from a Microsoft reseller at full
   price. Digital is not authorized to sell a Windows NT 3.1 to Windows NT
   3.51 Upgrade Kit. Restrictions may apply.

o  Users who wish to purchase additional Client Access Licenses for Windows
   NT 3.51 can purchase these through an authorized Microsoft reseller or
   through the Select Service program. Users will not be required to update
   the current 3.5 Client Access Licenses until the next major release.

TECHNICAL DATA

Windows NT Workstation 3.51 minimum system requirements:

o  Personal computer with a 386/25 or higher processor or a RISC based
   system
o  12 MB memory (16 MB for RISC based systems)
o  CD-ROM driver required, with one 3.5 inch high-density disk drive for
   boot disks
o  90 MB of available hard-disk space (120 MB for RISC based systems)
o  VGA, Super VGA, or high-resolution video graphics adapter
o  Network adapter card
o  Microsoft mouse or compatible pointing device

Windows NT Server 3.51 minimum system requirements:

o  Personal computer with a 386/25 or higher processor or a RISC based
   system
o  16 MB memory
o  CD-ROM driver required, with one 3.5 inch high-density disk drive for
   boot disks
o  90 MB of available hard-disk space (120 MB for RISC based systems)
o  VGA, Super VGA, or high-resolution video graphics adapter
o  Network adapter card
o  Microsoft mouse or compatible pointing device

Note: Refer to the Windows NT 3.51 Hardware Compatibility Guide for more
      details.

New features

New features of Windows NT Workstation 3.51 are:

o  Setup
   - 5.25 inch setup disks removed from kit
   - Unattended setup eliminates the needs for setup floppy disks and allows
     users to install or upgrade without being present
   - Floating-point division error exhibited in some Intel Pentium
     processors is detected and can be corrected during Setup

o  Windows 95 Common Control and Help are supported in File Manager, Print
   Manager, Clipboard Viewer, Command Prompt, Chat, CD Player, Media Player,
   and Sound Recorder.

o  Increased support for certain Personal Computer Memory Cards
   International Association (PCMCIA) cards. Refer to the Windows NT 3.51
   Hardware Compatibility List for complete listing.

o  Books Online allows users to point to the location of the online Windows
   NT Workstation or Windows NT Server manuals.

o  New Control Panel Console options allow users to change the appearance
   and position of character-based and command prompt windows.

o  Command Line Utilities include format and route and three new
   command-line utilities:
   - pentnt -- Checks floating-point division error
   - ntbooks -- Books Online utility
   - compact -- Displays and alters the compression of files on NTFS
     partitions

o  Command Prompt

o  File Manager offers new dialog box added to change tray/form assignment
   of a PostScript printer.

o  Maximum registry size can be changed using the systems option in Control
   Panel.

o  Schedule Service -- cmd command does not load by default

o  Sound Recorder -- new Properties command has been added

o  New functionality enables Telnet to output command operations to a log
   file.

o  Uninterruptible power supply (UPS) -- Administrators cannot specify
   command files that require user input.

o  User Profile Editor V allows Logon scripts to complete execution before
   Program Manager starts.

In addition to the Windows NT Workstation 3.51 features listed above,
Windows NT Server 3.51 offers:

o  Setup
   - Choose Licensing Mode -- Select licensing mode and agree to terms of
     the licensing agreement.
   - Per Serve Option -- Each Client Access License is assigned to a
     particular server and allows one connection to that server for basic
     network services (file, print, and communications).  Connection is made
     to the server; either individual shares or printers on a single server
     are considered only one connection for licensing purposes.
  -  Per Seat Option -- This licensing mode requires a Client Access License
     for each computer that will access Windows NT Server for basic network
     services (file, print, and communications). Once a computer is
     licensed, it may be used to access any Windows NT Server computer at no
     additional charge. A separate Client Access License is required for
     each computer, including Windows for Workgroups, Microsoft Windows NT
     Workstation, third-party vendors, or any of the other client software
     supported by Windows NT Server.

o  Licensing Tool  in Control Panel -- Tool to change licensing mode on that
   local computer from Per Server to Per Seat (one-time only). Also used to
   configure licensing replication for that computer.

o  License Manager Program in the Network Administration program group
   provides centralized view of licenses across the organization, manages
   the purchasing or deleting of licenses for products on network servers
   over which they have administrative rights, views usage statistics per
   user, and balances the licensing replication load across the network.

o  User Manager for Domains -- User profile paths can be assigned to the
   user account in the security database of a Windows NT Workstation.

o  Third Party Network File System (NFS) client software with Windows NT
   Workstation 3.1 or Windows NT Server 3.1 requires an update from an NFS
   vendor to run Version 3.51 on Windows NT Workstation 3.51 and Windows NT
   Server 3.51.

