PATHWORKS Support for Windows 95

HIGHLIGHTS

o  PATHWORKS software supports Microsoft's Windows 95 operating system on
   the day of release

o  "Protected mode" implementation ensures conventional memory on the
   desktop is freed for other application usage

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital is introducing PATHWORKS software support for Microsoft's Windows 95
operating system on the day of its release.  PATHWORKS will support Windows
95 through client support and server support.

The initial release of the PATHWORKS client software for Windows 95 focuses
on providing users with connectivity to their PATHWORKS servers. The new,
specially designed PATHWORKS client software for Windows 95 is an entirely
"protected mode" implementation, which means that precious conventional
memory on the desktop is freed for other application usage. DECnet, LAT,
CTERM, and Telnet network transports are included in the initial release of
PATHWORKS for Windows 95, offering connectivity to a PATHWORKS network. Also
included in the initial release are applications designed for connectivity
purposes -- VT320 for host-based communications and Mosaic for Internet
browsing and information searching.

PATHWORKS server software now supports incoming file and print connections
from Windows 95 desktops.

BENEFITS

As PATHWORKS users deploy Windows 95 in their networks, it is critical that
they retain access to their PATHWORKS servers to accomplish their daily
work. The PATHWORKS client software designed for Windows 95 enables users to
deploy Windows 95 now. Users will experience no delay in deploying or
migrating to the new operating system, and will experience no productivity
loss.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The right to use this initial release of PATHWORKS client software for
Windows 95 is included with one of the following software licenses:
PATHWORKS V5.1 for DOS and Windows (LAN Manager) CCS, PATHWORKS V5.1 for DOS
and Windows (NetWare) CCS, and PATHWORKS V5.1 for DOS and Windows CNS.

Users holding licenses for earlier versions of PATHWORKS for DOS and Windows
are required to purchase upgrade licenses to PATHWORKS V5.1 client software.
Refer to the PATHWORKS V5.1 for DOS and Windows Software Product Description
(SPD 55.07.15) for the list of PATHWORKS client license part numbers.

Users holding Media and Documentation Distribution Service (MDDS) contracts
will automatically receive the PATHWORKS client software for Windows 95.
Users with PATHWORKS V5.1 client licenses who do not have an MDDS service
contract can order the software. The documentation is included in an online
format on the CD-ROM and is integrated into the Windows 95 help system to
ensure compatibility with the Windows 95 operating system.

PATHWORKS server licensing and software

Users who do not require any PATHWORKS client software (e.g., DECnet and
LAT) on their Windows 95 systems, but do require access to PATHWORKS
