FYI Subjects

IN THIS ISSUE

o  Release Strategy for DECnet/OSI for OpenVMS
o  PCI RAID and SCSI Controllers for Prioris Servers

RELEASE STRATEGY FOR DECNET/OSI FOR OPENVMS

With the next release of DECnet/OSI for OpenVMS software, the release
schedule for this product will move from a release each quarter to a release
every other quarter. This change will allow a major and a minor DECnet/OSI
for OpenVMS release each year to incorporate new features and code
modifications.

This new policy will increase the support period for each release to at
least 12 months: six months as the current release and six months as the
previous release. Where required by a major operating system version release
(e.g., OpenVMS V7.0), support for the final version of DECnet/OSI for
OpenVMS software on the older operating system version will be extended
further to ensure sufficient support while the user base is upgrading to the
new operating system.

These new guidelines will ensure adequate support levels for user
satisfaction, ensure adequate support periods for DECnet/OSI for OpenVMS
releases, provide code fixes in a timely manner without incurring extra
release cycles, and minimize the number of version streams supported at any
one time

In all cases, where a problem is known to be resolved, users reporting
instances of that problem will be requested to upgrade to the version where
the fix exists. Fixes will not be retrofitted to releases that are no longer
supported. ECO kits will continue to be the vehicle for shipping critical
fixes between formal releases.

PCI RAID AND SCSI CONTROLLERS FOR PRIORIS SERVERS

Digital has introduced 1 and 3 channel PCI Fast and Wide RAID controllers
and the Adaptec 3940W 2 channel PCI Fast and Wide SCSI Controller for the
Prioris HX and Prioris XL Server lines.

The 1 channel and 3 channel controllers support 0, 1, and 5 RAID levels. The
1 channel controller is used for one RAID segment; the 3 channel controller
is used for internal and external RAID arrays. The 1 channel controller
supports seven wide or narrow SCSI drives, while the 3 channel controller
supports 21 wide or narrow SCSI drives. Both controllers include the
following operating system drivers: Windows NT, Windows NT Workstation 3.5
and Windows NT Server 3.5, NetWare 3.1X and 4.X, SCO UNIX System V Release
4.0, UnixWare System V release 4.2, and MS-DOS 5.0 and above.

The Adaptec 3940W 2 channel PCI Fast and Wide SCSI controller complements
the Prioris Server line with two independent channels that can transfer data
up to 40 MB per second. The controller supports seven devices per channel,
with wide or narrow (8 bit or 16 bit) device protocol. The controller will
work in the Windows NT, NetWare, SCO UNIX, UnixWare, and OS/2 operating
environments. These RAID and SCSI controllers are available now.

