POLYCENTER DECnet Manager V2.1

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Enhancements provide client/server capability for network managers
   managing DECnet environments as part of their multivendor and
   multiprotocol networks

*  Layers on POLYCENTER Manager on NetView V4.1 and integrates tightly with
   its graphical user interface, databases, and new features, such as
   client/server and event correlation

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

POLYCENTER DECnet Manager V2.1 for Digital UNIX software (SPD 62.53) is
available as a layered product on POLYCENTER Manager on NetView V4.1 for
Digital UNIX software (SPD 53.57). POLYCENTER DECnet Manager V2.1 consists
of network management applications to manage DECnet Phase IV using Network
Control Program (NCP), DECnet/OSI using Network Command Language (NCL),
Digital's LAN bridges using Remote Bridge Management Software (RBMS), and
Digital's terminal servers using Console Carrier Request (CCR). Additional
non-network management-specific functionality, such as data collection and
reference data applications, is also included in POLYCENTER DECnet Manager
V2.1.

POLYCENTER DECnet Manager V2.1 uses the same map and user interface
components as POLYCENTER Manager on NetView, which are acknowledged as the
industry's leading GUI for network management. Use of the General Topology
Manager API ensures close integration of DECnet and IP.

For more information on POLYCENTER Manager on NetView V4.1 for Digital UNIX
software, see the "POLYCENTER Manager on NetView V4.1 for Digital UNIX"
article in the August 8 online issue of Customer Update.

Product enhancements

POLYCENTER DECnet Manager V2.1 allows the management station to run in a
client/server environment. The client portion can be installed on a separate
system (or several systems) from the server component, allowing multiple
users to monitor and manage the same network. This client/server function
allows user-oriented portions of the network management process to be
distributed. The view seen by the user can be customized by user or by
function, and the client system can offload some processing from the server.

