Digital DCE V1.1 for Windows NT

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Use of Microsoft Remote Procedure Call requires less memory for
   applications

*  Supports building DCE applications in C++ on both Intel and Alpha Windows
   NT platforms

*  Provides direct access to DCE security services through Generic Security
   Service API

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Digital DCE V1.1 for Windows NT product family provides the Windows NT
implementation of the distributed computing functionality specified by the
Open Software Foundation (OSF). Digital DCE V1.1 for Windows NT consists of
DCE Runtime Services, a DCE Application Development Kit, a DCE Cell
Directory Server, and a DCE Security Server -- all of which use the
Microsoft Remote Procedure Call (RPC) mechanism to communicate between
processes. This mechanism interoperates fully with DCE clients or servers
running on any vendor's platform. In addition, with Windows NT 3.51,
Microsoft RPC now supports authenticated remote procedure calls over the
UDP/IP (datagram) transport. Use of the Microsoft RPC requires less memory
for DCE applications based on Digital's DCE products.

The DCE Application Development Kit has been extended to support development
of DCE applications in C++ on both Intel and Alpha Windows NT platforms.
This support is only available from Digital at this time. Digital is
supplying this technology to the Open Software Foundation (OSF) for future
industry releases of DCE.  Digital DCE V1.1 for Windows NT also supports the
Generic Security Service API (GSSAPI). This API allows applications that
need security services, but do not use the RPC mechanism, to access the DCE
security services directly. In addition, Digital DCE V1.1 for Windows NT
contains an integrated login feature that allows users who routinely log in
to a DCE cell from Windows NT to use a single login to access both their
Windows NT and DCE accounts.

