DECswitch 900 Router For DEChub 900 MultiSwitch

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Key component of Digital's enVISN network architecture

*  Routing now on Ethernet and FDDI switches

*  DEChub 900 MultiSwitch forms virtual LANs between routes

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital's enVISN architecture combines virtual LAN technology, distributed
routing, and high-speed switching. The DECswitch 900EE and DECswitch 900EF
are key components of that architecture. They lay the foundation for
designing virtual LANs and virtual switched networks. The DECswitch 900EE
and 900EF are the only products on the market today that combine switching
and routing technologies in a flexible hub module.  This combination of
switched networks and virtual LANs can dynamically configure a flexible,
scalable, and manageable network for large sites and mobile working groups.

The DECswitch 900 family of Ethernet and Ethernet/FDDI switches provides
level 2 switching for high-performance bridging, or level 3 routing for LAN
segmentation and inter-VLAN routing. Two models are available:

*    DECswitch 900EE has six Ethernet ports
*    DECswitch 900EF has six Ethernet ports and one FDDI.

All the ports can be configured to the DEChub Multiswitch backplane or are
accessible through front panel connections.

BENEFITS

*  Virtual LAN -- The DECswitch 900 routes traffic between virtual LANs
   formed with PORTswitches within the DEChub MultiSwitch. Users can be
   grouped within their own virtual LANs to ensure high-speed connectivity

*  Distributed routing EPA --  Provides better performance, reliability,
   scalability, and interoperability than other centralized routing
   architectures because full routing function is built into hubs, switches,
   access routers, and central site routers

*  LAN hopping -- Through the HUBwatch management systems, users can
   configure an of the six Ethernet ports and the single FDDI port on a
   per-port basis, to be accessible via the either from the front panel or
   the Ethernet and FDDI rails in the DEChub MultiSwitch.

*  Large address space -- By supporting over 8,000 node addresses, the
   network manager can build a network infrastructure using shared and
   dedicated LANs

*  SNMP support -- Allows monitoring from SNMP Network Management Stations

*  Flash memory -- Provides easy, non-disruptive software upgrades over the
   network from any BOOT/TFTP host

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The DECswitch 900 EE/EF Router will be available on September 8, 1995 from
Digital and through authorized VARs, distributors, and master resellers.

For the initial purchase of a DECswitch 900EE or a DECswitch 900EF router,
use the DEFBA-** and the DEBMP-** option numbers shown below. These order
numbers are complete packages that include the hardware unit with the
