ATMworks 350 ATM Interface Card

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Joins the ATMworks 750 ATM interface card as the industry's fastest ATM
   adapters at 155 Mbits per second (OC3) ATM network speed

*  Multimode fiber cable interface and SONET/SDH framing

*  Supports ATM Adaptation Layer 5 (AAL5)

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The ATMworks 350 ATM interface card provides PCI-to-ATM connectivity for any
PCI Alpha based system. It allows high bandwidth connections for servers and
high performance workstations to connect to a high performance network
(ATM), enabling data to be exchanged quickly with minimal latency. The
interface card also enables the use of systems for multimedia network
applications by taking advantage of the guaranteed bandwidth and low latency
capabilities of ATM networks. This product allows users to transmit and
receive images efficiently over various distances using ATM networks.

BENEFITS

When used as servers, systems can take advantage of a high bandwidth ATM
network to serve multiple clients, thereby reducing delays and relieving
network congestion.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The ATMworks 350 is available now through Digital and its business partners.

Order No.         Description

DGLPB-AB          ATMworks 350 PCI to ATM adapter

TECHNICAL DATA

*  Provides an industry standard 32 bit PCI interface to the host processor

*  Is standards compliant -- meets FCC Class B standards and CE-Mark
   approval

*  Maximum throughput of the ATMworks 350 is a factor of the protocol
   stacks, packet sizes, I/O bus loading, and relative CPU power. At the
   driver/data-link level, the ATMworks 350 is capable of achieving data
   rates in excess of 130 Mbits per second.

*  Connects to 155 Mbits per second ATM networks that use SONET/SDH framing
   using 62.5/125 multimode fiber optic cable systems

*  Supports 2048 Virtual Circuits (VCs)

*  With Digital UNIX, provides Unassigned Bit Rate (UBR) class of service

*  Supports ATM Adaptation Layer 5 (AAL5) in hardware

*  Supports FLOWmaster flow control, which together with the GIGAswitch/ATM
   system, eliminates cell loss due to network congestion, maximizes network
   utilization, and ensures network stability

*  Supported by Digital UNIX V3.2C, which provides classical IP support per
   RFC 1577 and Q.2931 signaling, is UNI 3.0 compliant, and delivers
   Permanent Virtual Circuits (PVCs) and Switched Virtual Circuits (SVCs).
   LAN Emulation Client will be available in the next release of Digital
   UNIX.

*  Uses a packet-based interface to the host to eliminate host processing of
   cells, which increases performance and minimizes host utilization.

Hardware requirements

*  Digital PCI based Alpha system
*  One full size 32 bit PCI slot
*  Interface cable (62.5/125 multimode fiber cable with SC connector)
*  ATM switch, such as the GIGAswitch/ATM system

Software requirements

*  Digital UNIX V3.2C or later

Configuration rules

*  One ATMworks 350 adapter is supported per system on the Digital UNIX
   platform. Support for multiple adapters is planned for the future.

*  The ATMworks 350 is only supported in single processor systems on the
   Digital UNIX platform. Support for multiprocessor configurations is
   planned for the future.

*  The ATMworks 350 should be used in systems that use only 5V universal
   signaling modules, and not with those systems that use 3.3V signaling
   modules.

*  The ATMworks 350 can be connected to an ATM network via an ATM switch
   that meets the UNI 3.0 and OC3 specifications, such as the GIGAswitch/ATM
   system.

*  The Alpha system in which the ATMworks 350 will be installed must have
   the correct revision of the console software. The correct revision for
   each system is:
   - AlphaServer 1000 -- V3.1 or later
   - AlphaServer 2000, 2100 -- V4.1 or later
   - AlphaServer 8200, 8400 -- V2.0 or later
   - AlphaStation 200, 400 -- V1.1-3 or later
   - AlphaStation 250 4/266 -- V5.0 or later
   - AlphaStation 600 -- V1.1-13 or later



