NetWare Connectivity for IBM, Digital, and UNIX Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Integrates NetWare networks with Digital, IBM and UNIX systems

o  Includes unlimited client license; unlimited session license

o  Eliminates the need for multiple-protocol stacks in client PCs

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Forest Computer, a leading manufacturer of interconnectivity products and
gateways for the IBM/Digital/UNIX market, has released Forest High-Function
Gateway for NetWare, to be marketed under its TOEM agreement with Digital.
It uses Alpha technology to deliver NetWare interconnectivity services to
OpenVMS, ULTRIX, UNIX, PATHWORKS TCP/IP, IBM SNA 2.0, and IBM SNA 2.1
environments. The Forest gateway is a comprehensive solution for
interconnecting with

*  VAX, Alpha, DECserver, and DECsystem computers via DECnet LAN links
*  AIX, AS/400, System/36, and System/38 computers via Advanced Peer-to-Peer
   Networking (APPN) and advanced Program-to-Program (APPC) LAN or WAN links
*  IBM VM, MVS, and VSE mainframes via Systems Network Architecture (SNA)
   LAN or WAN links
*  A wide variety of UNIX systems including Digital UNIX, HP-UX, AIX, and
   Solaris
*  SCO, AT&T, and BSD implementation via TCP/IP LAN links

The Forest High-Function Gateway allows NetWare clients to initiate terminal
sessions to any of these hosts over IPX, which eliminates the need for
multiple protocol stacks in client PCs. NetWare clients can initiate file
transfers between any of these hosts using the standard DOS "copy" command
or Windows File Manager. Host systems can also initiate file transfers using
native transfer facilities. Printer sharing is equally seamless because host
printers appear as NetWare print servers.

BENEFITS

The Forest gateway is strategically positioned as an alternative to the
gateway products offered by Novell and Microsoft. The gateway

*  Includes client-side software for VT-, 5250-, and 3270-based terminal
   emulation and does not require additional client software for file
   transfer or printer sharing.

*  Supports concurrent NetWare connectivity to DECnet, TCP/IP, SNA, or
   APPC/APPN networks.

*  The Forest gateway is sold on a flat-fee license. No user-based or
   session-based charges are applied and no third-party client-side software
   is required.

*  Operates on an Alpha platform. which offers superior performance over
   Intel-based gateways.

*  Includes remote diagnostic capabilities for comprehensive end-to-end
   support. Forest support personnel, trained on all host and network
   variations, can dial into the gateway and diagnose problems anywhere in
   the network.

*  Dedicates a turnkey gateway. No additional layered software is required
   on any of the interconnected hosts. All the NetWare client software is
   included.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Alpha-based version of the Forest High-Function Gateway for NetWare is
available now. Consult your Digital or third-party sales representative for
the terms and conditions of Digital's agreement with Forest Computer.

SERVICES

Contact Forest Computer for configuration assistance and a product quote.

