SCO OPENSERVER RELEASE 5 SYSTEMS

SCO OpenServer software is today's leading UNIX server operating system for
Intel processor-based platforms. SCO OpenServer systems are exceptional at
running multiuser, transaction-based DBMS and business applications,
communications gateways, and mail and messaging servers in both host and
client/server environments.

The SCO OpenServer Development System is comprised of a core set of
development tools that enable software developers to rapidly build, test,
and deploy business critical solutions on the SCO OpenServer Host System,
SCO OpenServer Enterprise System, and SCO OpenServer Desktop System. The SCO
OpenServer Development System is comprised of a set of state-of-the-art
compilers, debuggers, application programming interfaces (APIs), and
libraries needed to develop business critical applications.

The SCO OpenServer Host System is an ideal platform for organizations
downsizing mini or mainframe computing environments for replicated
organizations, including retail stores, food franchises, banks, and hotels,
and for small-to-medium sized businesses that cannot yet justify the
additional expense and support of networked PCs and client/server network
architectures.

In addition to supporting host based UNIX system applications and character
terminals, the SCO OpenServer Enterprise System supports client/server
applications and environments consisting of Windows PCs, UNIX system
workstations, X terminals, and other servers and clients over a variety of
networks. The Enterprise System delivers all the necessary facilities for
running high performance, transaction-based DBMS and business applications,
communications gateways, and mail and messaging servers in client/server
environments.

